# Proverb list (English) -- one proverb per line, separated by a line feed.
#
# Read by src/lib/randomLine.js, which streams the file and returns one randomly
# chosen line without loading it. The WeatherMan automation draws from here when
# `add_proverb: true` is set in etc/automation/tts-weatherman.yaml, filling the
# {% proverb %} token of the weatherman bundle's ai_proverb / tts_proverb keys.
#
# Format rules (enforced by the reader, not by YAML):
#   - exactly one proverb per line, no quoting, no numbering
#   - blank lines are skipped, so you can group visually with empty lines
#   - a trailing newline at end of file is fine and never yields an empty proverb
#   - a '#' comment is NOT supported -- a comment line would be read as a proverb
#
# Copy this file to "proverbs.txt" in the same directory, then add your own
# lines below; the shipped set is a clean starting point.
A stitch in time saves nine.
Don't count your chickens before they hatch.
Fortune favours the bold.
